# Every checkout `just repos-apply` registers with `onevcs`, one path per line.
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored; a leading `~` expands against `$HOME`.
# Registration resolves each path's own `origin` to a repository identity, so the
# policy a checkout gets comes from `config/onevcs.rules.yml` matching that
# identity — not from anything written here. Several checkouts of one origin (a
# canonical checkout, a safety clone, an execution clone) therefore share one
# policy by construction.
#
# Always list the path. `onevcs` derives the alias from the checkout's directory
# name; an `owner/name` spelling passed here would be resolved as a GitHub
# repository of that name instead. See `docs/host-setup.md`.
#
# A path this host does not have is reported as skipped rather than failing the
# run, so a second machine registers the checkouts it does have.

# This repository: the publication checkout, then the two safety clones every
# self-dispatch executes in.
~/ai-orchestrator
~/ai-orchestrator-isolated
~/ai-orchestrator-isolated-2

# The published CLIs this repository configures.
~/projects/oneagentgraph
~/projects/onepipeline
~/projects/onepipeline-ui
~/projects/onevcs
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__oneharness
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__oneharness-ui
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__onejudge

# Other repositories dispatched against from this host.
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__crozier
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__dero-skills
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__nick-derobertis-site
~/.ai-orchestrator/repos/nickderobertis__screencomp
~/projects/org-apps
